# The menus on a desktop (1366 x 768): How to Play, Settings (the game's own options),
# the mode select with the Practice options, a Practice game's first turn (draw, undo,
# hint, a card picked by the arrows and Enter, the status rail), pause, Help from the
# pause menu and back, leaving the match; then Learn's first lesson completed by a draw.
# viewport 1366x768
until 600 Daily Challenge
frames 30
save title
click =How to Play
until 60 Controls
frames 10
expect Discard & deadwood
save help
click =Back
until 60 Daily Challenge
frames 10
click =Settings
until 60 Captions for sounds
frames 10
save settings
click =Left-handed controls
frames 10
click =Done
until 60 Daily Challenge
frames 10
click =Play
until 60 Choose a mode
frames 10
click =Practice
frames 10
expect Expected duration
click =50
frames 20
click =100
frames 20
save mode-practice
click =Start
until 300 Draw deck
frames 60
expect first to 100 points
save practice-table
click =Draw deck
frames 10
expect Your turn — meld / discard
click =Undo
frames 10
expect Your turn — draw
click =Hint
frames 10
expect Hint:
save hint
key KeyD 1
frames 10
key ArrowRight 1
frames 5
key ArrowRight 1
frames 5
key Enter 1
frames 10
save keyboard-pick
key Escape 1
frames 10
expect Your turn — meld / discard
key Escape 1
until 60 Resume
frames 10
save pause-dialog
click =Help
until 60 Controls
frames 10
click =Back
until 60 Draw deck
frames 10
click =Pause
until 60 Resume
frames 10
click =Settings
until 60 Captions for sounds
frames 10
click =Done
until 60 Resume
frames 10
click =Leave match
until 120 Daily Challenge
frames 10
click =Learn
until 300 Drawing a card
frames 30
save lesson
click =Take discard
frames 30
expect Your turn — meld / discard
